tu/a750: emit BR-only RB CCU registers outside CP_SET_THREAD_BOTH

Host-side half of Droid-VM/mesa 91be6906972 (author: lateautumn233).
RB is a BR-only hardware block on A7XX. Emitting the static RB_CCU_CNTL
write (and the RB_CCU_DBG_ECO_CNTL raw-magic entry) from
tu6_init_static_regs(), which runs under CP_SET_THREAD_BOTH and is also
reused by the BV bin-restore preamble, makes the BV pipeline replay
writes to registers that do not exist on BV, raising a per-frame CP AHB
bus error on a750/gen7_9 (RB_CCU_CNTL, offset 0x8e07, in kgsl dmesg).
Not upstream as of mesa 7f196910eb3. The guest-side half of that commit
(virtio FD750 chip ids) stays in Droid-VM/mesa -- it has no meaning for
a kgsl host driver.

Context regenerated against mesa 7f196910eb35aca76cf58d0c572c72c099e971a2.

